    {
      "title": "Air Chief Marshal Ashutosh Dixit takes charge as new Chief of Air Staff",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/air-chief-marshal-ashutosh-dixit-takes-charge-as-new-chief-of-air-staff-126103100759_1.html",
      "description": "Air Chief Marshal Ashutosh Dixit, an accomplished fighter pilot with over 3,500 hours of flying experience on over 20 types of aircraft, on Saturday assumed charge as the new Chief of Air Staff.\nHe succeeded Air Chief Marshal A P Singh who superannuated from the force after a 43-year-long illustrious career.\nThe IAF accorded a ceremonial guard of honour to Air Chief Marshal Singh at the Race Course Air Force Station before he handed over the baton to Dixit.\nAir Chief Marshal Dixit, known for his strategic planning and who played a key role during Operation Sindoor, was serving as the Vice Chief of the force.\nIn a distinguished career spanning four decades, Air Chief Marshal Dixit has held a variety of Command, Staff and Instructional appointments.\nBorn on December 9, 1966, Air Marshal Ashutosh Dixit was commissioned into the fighter stream of the Indian Air Force on December 6, 1986.\nPrior to assuming charge as the Vice Chief of the Air Staff, Air Chief Marshal Dixit served as Ch",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-31T09:48:11"
    }
